# {Topic} — Experimental Protocol & Results

## 1. Experimental Environment & Apparatus
* **Compute Infrastructure:** 8x NVIDIA H100 SXM5, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, PyTorch 2.4 / CUDA 12.4.
* **Dataset / Workload:** Standardized benchmark corpus ($100,000$ sequence evaluations).
* **Control Against Bias:** Deterministic PRNG seed ($42$), cold cache runs before each benchmark suite.

## 2. Experimental Data Results
| Condition | Mean Metric ($p50$) | Tail Metric ($p99$) | Standard Deviation | Statistically Significant? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Baseline** | $124.2\text{ms}$ | $245.0\text{ms}$ | $\sigma = 14.1$ | Baseline |
| **Treatment A** | $88.5\text{ms}$ | $142.1\text{ms}$ | $\sigma = 8.2$ | Yes ($p = 0.0002$) |

## 3. Threat to Validity & Mitigations
* **Internal Validity:** Thermal throttling mitigated via fixed GPU fan curves and power caps.
* **External Validity:** Tested across 4 distinct domains to prevent domain overfitting.
